I get what you are saying and I agree with it, but I want to fully explore this to make sure there can be absolutely no other interpretation.

&nbsp;

The Augmented Ally &quot;optional trigger&quot; is <em>At the start of that hero&#39;s turn, their player may discard a card</em>.

You don&#39;t have to discard, it is your choice. It is the start of the turn. The player has discarded a card, satisfying the trigger.

&nbsp;

[quote=&quot;Parse&#39;s Critical Multiplier&quot;]Whenever you discard a card from hand, select a hero target. Increase the next damage dealt by that target by 1.[/quote][quote=&quot;Parse&#39;s Snap Decision&quot;]At the start of your turn, you may discard 1 card. If you do, you may play a card.[/quote]

At the start of the turn, Parse&#39;s player discards 1 card allowing a card to be played. The discarding gets co-opted to Critical Multiplier to apply its effect. Yes, the &quot;whenever&quot; is the persistant pass-through, the argument that I am making is that a single discard is activating the effects on two separate cards.

&nbsp;

Augmented Ally #1 allows for a card to be discarded. Where in the timing does a &quot;discarded card&quot; exist then cease to exist for the purposes of satisfying Augmented Ally #2?

